<title>UK: French Total to drill offshore Ireland.</title>
<headline>French Total to drill offshore Ireland.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>French oil group Total SA said it planned in early June to start drilling an exploration well in Ireland's offshore Porcupine basin.</p>
<p>The well, 150 km off southwest Ireland's Kerry coast, will be Total's first in block 35/17, licensed as part of the 1995 Porcupine basin exploration round.</p>
<p>Total is partnered in the block by Conoco, a unit of DuPont Co and DSM NV.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 17 542 8060</p>
